Fresh Wall Street Journal reporting published 18 Sep 2026 documents a
July 2026 authorized bug-bounty investigation by Hacktron AI.
Researchers found an OpenAI community-forum/Discourse flaw that
exposed authentication tokens. The tokens were reportedly valid beyond
the forum context, including access to ChatGPT and an OpenAI GitHub
repository; the researchers demonstrated access with a benign pull
request. OpenAI confirmed the issues, fixed them, and paid a $6,500
bounty. No monetary loss is established.

